{"id":"twitter:1817256423258239315","tweet_id":"1817256423258239315","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1817256423258239315","title":"I have been reading US Code, crime stats, and civil law trying to find out if being scraped by a bullet fragment is considered a gun shot wound. A fra","summary":"I have been reading US Code, crime stats, and civil law trying to find out if being scraped by a bullet fragment is considered a gun shot wound. A fragment can be considered a bullet wound if: -It is a major wound -Obvious exit and entrance wound Can real lawyers confirm?","date":"2024-07-27","published":"2024-07-27T17:51:08+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>I have been reading US Code, crime stats, and civil law trying to find out if being scraped by a bullet fragment is considered a gun shot wound.<br><br>A fragment can be considered a bullet wound if:<br><br>-It is a major wound<br>-Obvious exit and entrance wound<br><br>Can real lawyers confirm?</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1817256423258239315","display_date":"July 27, 2024 · 17:51 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
