{"id":"twitter:1816254193877016728","tweet_id":"1816254193877016728","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816254193877016728","title":"@dianesbaker1 @LongAsUCan2 @RickPetree Well wrote a few books on subject and wrote an approved curriculum for the DoD to to train third party assessor","summary":"@dianesbaker1 @LongAsUCan2 @RickPetree Well wrote a few books on subject and wrote an approved curriculum for the DoD to to train third party assessors to assess how people engineer trustworthiness in systems with Gov assets Folks are trying https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/certified-cmmc-assessor-handbook-j-gregory-mcverry/1144947862","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T23:28:38+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/dianesbaker1/status/1816251012858142752","reply_tweet_id":"1816251012858142752","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@dianesbaker1 @LongAsUCan2 @RickPetree Well wrote a few books on subject and wrote an approved curriculum for the DoD to to train third party assessors to assess how people engineer trustworthiness in systems with Gov assets<br><br>Folks are trying<br><br><a href=\"https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/certified-cmmc-assessor-handbook-j-gregory-mcverry/1144947862\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/certified-cmmc-assessor-handbook-j-gregory-mcverry/1144947862</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816254193877016728","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 23:28 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1816249363863163363","tweet_id":"1816249363863163363","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816249363863163363","title":"@dianesbaker1 And NIST-SP-800-171 only covers confidentiality. The integrity and availability of your system isn't a worry to the Gov unless it compro","summary":"@dianesbaker1 And NIST-SP-800-171 only covers confidentiality. The integrity and availability of your system isn't a worry to the Gov unless it compromises their data. If you are interested in how RMF works in Gov I'll send you some NIST-SP-800-53 classes. Free and good","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T23:09:27+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816248829701750889","reply_tweet_id":"1816248829701750889","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@dianesbaker1 And NIST-SP-800-171 only covers confidentiality. The integrity and availability of your system isn&#x27;t a worry to the Gov unless it compromises their data.<br><br>If you are interested in how RMF works in Gov I&#x27;ll send you some NIST-SP-800-53 classes.<br><br>Free and good</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816249363863163363","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 23:09 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1816248829701750889","tweet_id":"1816248829701750889","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816248829701750889","title":"@dianesbaker1 My state of Connecticut has 3,000 contractors for the Department of Defense alone. How many of billions of endpoints would your ERM have","summary":"@dianesbaker1 My state of Connecticut has 3,000 contractors for the Department of Defense alone. How many of billions of endpoints would your ERM have to touch to cover every single contractor that stores, transmits, or processes Gov assets? I don't want the Gov with that access.","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T23:07:19+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/dianesbaker1/status/1816248007375085674","reply_tweet_id":"1816248007375085674","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@dianesbaker1 My state of Connecticut has 3,000 contractors for the Department of Defense alone.<br><br>How many of billions of endpoints would your ERM have to touch to cover every single contractor that stores, transmits, or processes Gov assets?<br><br>I don&#x27;t want the Gov with that access.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816248829701750889","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 23:07 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
