{"id":"twitter:1816247293085131172","tweet_id":"1816247293085131172","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816247293085131172","title":"@dianesbaker1 What I said their risk based budgeting closer to your idea of universal ERM across Government that would fit within current regulatory e","summary":"@dianesbaker1 What I said their risk based budgeting closer to your idea of universal ERM across Government that would fit within current regulatory environment. And we didn't even mention FedRAMP and Cloud yet. Your solution, IMO, as someone working with ERMs in 171 systems is untenable","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T23:01:13+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/dianesbaker1/status/1816245469443678343","reply_tweet_id":"1816245469443678343","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@dianesbaker1 What I said their risk based budgeting closer to your idea of universal ERM across Government that would fit within current regulatory environment.<br><br>And we didn&#x27;t even mention FedRAMP and Cloud yet.<br><br>Your solution, IMO, as someone working with ERMs in 171 systems is untenable</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816247293085131172","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 23:01 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
