{"id":"twitter:1816046413177881000","tweet_id":"1816046413177881000","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816046413177881000","title":"Yes. Humans impacted Climate change last 100 years. From 1 billion to 35 million years ago humans couldn't impact climate. No humans.. For 35 million ","summary":"Yes. Humans impacted Climate change last 100 years. From 1 billion to 35 million years ago humans couldn't impact climate. No humans.. For 35 million years to about two hundred years ago we only impacted micro climates because no fossil fuel burning. Not hard to understand https://x.com/DeTocqueville14/status/1816043254732759174","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T09:43:00+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Yes.<br><br>Humans impacted Climate change last 100 years.<br><br>From 1 billion to 35 million years ago humans couldn&#x27;t impact climate. No humans..<br><br>For 35 million years to about two hundred years ago we only impacted micro climates because no fossil fuel burning.<br><br>Not hard to understand <a href=\"https://x.com/DeTocqueville14/status/1816043254732759174\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/DeTocqueville14/status/1816043254732759174</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816046413177881000","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 09:43 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
