{"id":"twitter:1816044747040923988","tweet_id":"1816044747040923988","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1816044747040923988","title":"@FixTechStuff1 @vxunderground Technically choosing Crowdstrike Falcon and not going all in on Microsoft Stack is choosing two vendors and not putting ","summary":"@FixTechStuff1 @vxunderground Technically choosing Crowdstrike Falcon and not going all in on Microsoft Stack is choosing two vendors and not putting all your eggs in one basket. If you had to meet Device encryption standards you didn't have to use Bitlocker, but still would have to unencrypt an asset","date":"2024-07-24","published":"2024-07-24T09:36:22+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/FixTechStuff1/status/1815662482255491409","reply_tweet_id":"1815662482255491409","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@FixTechStuff1 @vxunderground Technically choosing Crowdstrike Falcon and not going all in on Microsoft Stack is choosing two vendors and not putting all your eggs in one basket.<br><br>If you had to meet Device encryption standards you didn&#x27;t have to use Bitlocker, but still would have to unencrypt an asset</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1816044747040923988","display_date":"July 24, 2024 · 09:36 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
