{"id":"twitter:2039315080366428268","tweet_id":"2039315080366428268","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2039315080366428268","title":"@indigonl First poem of this year's drive: Listen to sand along our banks and hear us sing. Portraits of women of Wild Fields whose winds carry anthem","summary":"@indigonl First poem of this year's drive: Listen to sand along our banks and hear us sing. Portraits of women of Wild Fields whose winds carry anthems of our Steppes Slaves once harmonized tears of The Ruin Coalescing in Cacophonies of currents flowing along our river's edge Our songs… https://t.co/BpnN3nLFta","date":"2026-04-01","published":"2026-04-01T12:12:58+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/indigonl/status/2039218398068879641","reply_tweet_id":"2039218398068879641","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@indigonl First poem of this year&#x27;s drive:<br><br>Listen to sand along our banks<br>and hear us sing. Portraits of women of Wild Fields whose winds carry anthems of our Steppes<br> Slaves  once harmonized tears of<br>The Ruin<br> Coalescing in Cacophonies<br>of currents flowing along our river&#x27;s edge<br>Our songs… <a href=\"https://t.co/BpnN3nLFta\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/BpnN3nLFta</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/fadc47db512c18e18db338b6d1f31937.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2039315080366428268","display_date":"April 01, 2026 · 12:12 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/fadc47db512c18e18db338b6d1f31937.jpg"]}
