{"id":"twitter:1814268979780726823","tweet_id":"1814268979780726823","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1814268979780726823","title":"@JennGriffy Has @dougmillsnyt done a write up about how he got the picture? You need a camera set to 30,000fps to maybe capture a bullet. Who sets a c","summary":"@JennGriffy Has @dougmillsnyt done a write up about how he got the picture? You need a camera set to 30,000fps to maybe capture a bullet. Who sets a camera to 30,000fps to shoot a political rally? That makes no sense. Would love to learn about artist decision making process.","date":"2024-07-19","published":"2024-07-19T12:00:06+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/JennGriffy/status/1814267921419678048","reply_tweet_id":"1814267921419678048","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@JennGriffy Has @dougmillsnyt done a write up about how he got the picture?<br><br>You need a camera set to 30,000fps to maybe capture a bullet.<br><br>Who sets a camera to 30,000fps to shoot a political rally?<br><br>That makes no sense.<br><br>Would love to learn about artist decision making process.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1814268979780726823","display_date":"July 19, 2024 · 12:00 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
