{"id":"twitter:2086402571464282276","tweet_id":"2086402571464282276","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2086402571464282276","title":"@NicolaDawn5 @hottaspotta @tastevictory24 Interestingy enough the recipes developed independently but the UK adopted the American name in the 1950s, b","summary":"@NicolaDawn5 @hottaspotta @tastevictory24 Interestingy enough the recipes developed independently but the UK adopted the American name in the 1950s, but name took off in 1990s The UK version traces back to meat pastries of 19th century. The American version started with an oyster wrapped in bacon.","date":"2026-08-09","published":"2026-08-09T10:41:51+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/NicolaDawn5/status/2086353978770461017","reply_tweet_id":"2086353978770461017","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@NicolaDawn5 @hottaspotta @tastevictory24 Interestingy enough the recipes developed independently but the UK adopted the American name in the 1950s, but name took off in 1990s<br><br>The UK version traces back to meat pastries of 19th century. The American version started with an oyster wrapped in bacon.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2086402571464282276","display_date":"August 09, 2026 · 10:41 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
