{"id":"twitter:2038252629231309098","tweet_id":"2038252629231309098","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2038252629231309098","title":"@Restitutor_ Written a couple books on the basics of assessing NIST-SP-800-171 environments. In the United States of America any Government contractor","summary":"@Restitutor_ Written a couple books on the basics of assessing NIST-SP-800-171 environments. In the United States of America any Government contractor needs to protect the confidentiality of data that is not classified, but not meant for public release. That means meeting 171. https://t.co/TasefqZt38","date":"2026-03-29","published":"2026-03-29T13:51:10+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2038252086215754236","reply_tweet_id":"2038252086215754236","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Restitutor_ Written a couple books on the basics of assessing NIST-SP-800-171 environments.<br><br>In the United States of America any Government contractor needs to protect the confidentiality of data that is not classified, but not meant for public release.<br><br>That means meeting 171. <a href=\"https://t.co/TasefqZt38\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/TasefqZt38</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/51b0f58d59850d1ee1727d8e44c1cd7f.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2038252629231309098","display_date":"March 29, 2026 · 13:51 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/51b0f58d59850d1ee1727d8e44c1cd7f.jpg"]}
{"id":"twitter:2038252086215754236","tweet_id":"2038252086215754236","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2038252086215754236","title":"@Restitutor_ No, not really. Owned a SaaS company and fool around with PHP and Python for fun But I work in the Compliance space around NIST-SP-800-17","summary":"@Restitutor_ No, not really. Owned a SaaS company and fool around with PHP and Python for fun But I work in the Compliance space around NIST-SP-800-171 environments. I do a lot of Incident Response Tabletops I am not a dev, but need to be able to translate it for normies.","date":"2026-03-29","published":"2026-03-29T13:49:00+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/Restitutor_/status/2038249932021211567","reply_tweet_id":"2038249932021211567","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Restitutor_ No, not really.<br><br>Owned a SaaS company and  fool around with PHP and Python for fun<br><br>But I work in the Compliance space around NIST-SP-800-171 environments.<br><br>I do a lot of Incident Response Tabletops<br><br>I am not a dev, but need to be able to translate it for normies.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2038252086215754236","display_date":"March 29, 2026 · 13:49 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
